"H1419":"large","H8098":"Shemaiah","H2815":"Hasshub","H5840":"Azrikam","H2811":"Hashabiah","H1138":"Bunni","H7678":"Shabbethai","H3107":"Jozacar","H2435":"outer","H4983":"Mattaniah","H4318":"Micah","H2067":"Zabdi","H623":"Asaph","H8462":"beginning","H3034":"to give thanks","H8605":"prayer","H1229":"Bakbukiah","H5653":"Abda","H8051":"Shammua","H1559":"Galal","H3038":"Jeduthun","H8084":"eighty","H7778":"gatekeeper","H6126":"Akkub","H2929":"Talmon","H8104":"obey","H8179":"gate","H7657":"seventy","H5159":"inheritance","H6077":"Ophel","H6727":"Ziha","H1658":"Gishpa","H5813":"Uzzi","H1137":"Bani","H4316":"Mica","H7891":"to sing","H5048":"before","H3588":"for","H4687":"commandment","H4428":"king","H548":"sure","H1697":"word","H3117":"day","H6611":"Pethahiah","H4898":"Meshezabel","H2226":"Zerah","H413":"to(wards)","H2691":"court","H7704":"Sirion","H7153":"Kiriath-arba","H1323":"daughter","H1769":"Dibon","H3343":"Jekabzeel","H3442":"Jeshua","H4137":"Moladah","H1046":"Beth-pelet","H2705":"Hazar-shual","H884":"Beersheba","H6860":"Ziklag","H4368":"Meconah","H5884":"En-rimmon","H6881":"Zorah","H3412":"Jarmuth","H2182":"Zanoah","H5725":"Adullam","H3923":"Lachish","H5825":"Azekah","H2583":"to camp","H5704":"till","H1516":"Valley","H2011":"(Topheth of) Hinnom","H1387":"Geba","H4363":"Michmash","H5857":"Ai","H1008":"Bethel","H6068":"Anathoth","H5011":"Nob","H6055":"Ananiah","H2674":"Hazor","H7414":"Ramah","H1664":"Gittaim","H2307":"Hadid","H6650":"Zeboim","H5041":"Neballat","H3850":"Lod","H207":"Ono","H2791":"silently","H4256":"division"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Lots. Those who had a mind to fix their abode at Jerusalem, received every encouragement. But some were compelled, that the city might regain its ancient splendour, and become the bulwark of the nation. Josephus ([Antiquities?] xi. 5.) says, that Nehemias built at his own expense houses for the priest and Levites, who chose to reside there."],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Blessed. Applauding their zeal and disinterestedness, as the city was yet only a heap of ruins. (Calmet) — Some from the other ten tribes returned; but the transactions of three tribes are more particularly noticed. (Ven. Bede) (Worthington)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Solomon. See 1 Esdras ii. 55., and 1 Paralipomenon ix. 2."],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Benjamin, as well as of Ephraim and Manasses, 1 Paralipomenon ix. 3. The difference between this last record and the present, arises from Nehemias including many who returned with Esdras and with himself. (Calmet)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Silonite. Or the son of Sela, 1 Paralipomenon ix. 5. (Tirinus)"],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Second. Vicegerent of Joel, (Calmet) or commander of a second part of the city. (Syriac)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Achitob had the inspection over the Levites and treasures. Eliasib was then pontiff. (Calmet)"],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Amassai. Or (1 Paralipomenon ix. 12.) Maasai, the son of Adiel, the son of Jezra, the son of Mosollam, the son of Mosollamoth, the son of Emmer."],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","The mighty, for riches and power; on which account this family was conspicuous."],["haydock",15,null,"haydock","Semeia. The ancient Latin manuscripts read Sebenia. (Martinay.)"],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","Outward. For repairs of the temple, cultivation of the lands given by vow; also to buy provisions, sacred vestments, &c."],["haydock",17,null,"haydock","Praise. Master of music. (Calmet) — Hebrew, “chief to begin the thanksgiving in prayer.” Syriac, “leader of the Jews in prayer.” (Haydock)"],["haydock",21,null,"haydock","Gaspha, were chiefs of the Nathinites. (Calmet) — Hebrew, “over the,” &c. Ophel was their place of residence, chap. iii. 26."],["haydock",22,null,"haydock","Overseer. Literally, “bishop.” Hebrew pekid, which has the same meaning. (Haydock) — Christians styled him who was at the head, bishop; as the Athenians did their chief justice. (Grotius) (Estius) (Calmet)"],["haydock",23,null,"haydock","King’s. David’s, (chap. xii. 24,) or perhaps the Persian monarch, who had appointed a maintenance for the priests, &c., 1 Esdras vi., and vii. (Calmet) — Order. Hebrew, “that a certain portion should be for the singers, due for every day.” (Protestants)"],["haydock",24,null,"haydock","People. They addressed themselves to him, (Haydock) and he gave an exact account to the king (Calmet) of Persia. (Menochius)"],["haydock",25,null,"haydock","The houses. Hebrew, “and for the dwellings, (Calmet) or villages.” (Pagnin) (Menochius) — Villages. Literally, “daughters,” which is often used in this sense. (Haydock)"],["haydock",26,null,"haydock","Jesue. This, and many of the other cities, had changed names, or were not built in the time of Josue. (Calmet)"],["haydock",30,null,"haydock","Bersabee. The southern extremity of Juda, (Menochius) unto the valley on the east of Jerusalem. (Adrichomius 186.)"],["haydock",34,35,"haydock","Lod. Built by Samad, 1 Paralipomenon viii. 12. It is called Lod-Hadid, chap. vii. 37. — Ono had the same founder, and stood in the valley of craftsmen, chap. vi. 2., and 1 Paralipomenon iv. 14."],["haydock",36,null,"haydock","Portions. The Levites dwelt in the cities assigned to these two tribes. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}